# Windows Maintenance Center - build & tooling artefacts
# Release artefacts are reproducible and must never be committed.

# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/
artifacts/
release/
# The evidence area of chapter 71 is called "release" as well. The pattern above would swallow it,
# and a re-include of a file below an excluded directory is impossible in git - so the directory
# itself is re-included here. Without this line `test-results/release/` can never be committed,
# which is exactly how the tenth evidence area went missing (found by tools/check-evidence-layout.py
# on 2026-09-23: the folder existed on disk and was ignored by git).
!test-results/release/
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage*.xml
coverage*.json

# Test result files below test-results/ are evidence and must be committable. Without these lines a
# fresh *.trx would be ignored and the unit test area could only ever hold the files that were added
# before the rule existed (found on 2026-09-23). Build output stays ignored - the negation covers the
# evidence directory only.
!test-results/**/*.trx
!test-results/**/*.xml
!test-results/**/*.json
!test-results/**/*.jsonl

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/
packages/
# Central package management lock file is committed on purpose (reproducible restore)
# packages.lock.json is NOT ignored.

# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.DotSettings.user

# MSBuild
*.binlog
*.metaproj
*.metaproj.tmp

# Inno Setup output
installer/Output/
*.iss.bak

# Portable/runtime data (never commit local machine state)
*.dmp
*.etl
*.hglocal

# Python-Werkzeuge: von den Prüfskripten erzeugte Caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
